suggestions.suggestion:
There is a tiny TOCTOU window between checkDeadline (line 312) and Duration.between(Instant.now(), deadline) (line 313): if the VT is descheduled for >0ms in between, remainingMs can come back slightly negative. Today's code handles this correctly — Math.min(positiveDurationMs, negativeRemainingMs) yields a negative actualMs, the `if (actualMs > 0)` guard skips the sleep, and the post-check at line 323 throws the timeout exception. So the behavior is correct, but the intermediate negative value is mildly surprising to readers. A `Math.max(0L, ...)` clamp on remainingMs would make the invariant explicit without changing observable behavior:

  long remainingMs = Math.max(0L, Duration.between(Instant.now(), deadline).toMillis());
  long actualMs = Math.min(durationMs, remainingMs);

Strictly cosmetic — no functional bug.
